Z||000000||bcwawright||07-18-2001||12:26 PM||||I am fixing to install a 3800 SeriesII Supercharged engine and was wanting to know who makes the BEST conversion kit. Also would like to know if there are some after market items to put on the motor to make more HP i.e. cam, headers,underdrive pulley, ignition coils and plug wires,clutch and flywheel, etc.<BR>Thanks for any help!!!!<P>Bruce<BR>88GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||West Coast Fiero||07-18-2001||01:20 PM||||check us out - <A HREF="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WCF%20page01.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WCF%20page01.htm</A> <P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||07-18-2001||05:18 PM||||Hey, that looks good!<P>Are you intercooling that engine?<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000003||West Coast Fiero||07-18-2001||06:39 PM||||It is not neccassary to intercool any turbocharged engine if under 7 lbs of boost, it will be pushing 6 lbs per customer request. However, we will be using a set of 3800 injectors to enter more fuel into the engine as the engine approaches WOT. Fuel has a much faster and effecient heat tranfer co-effecient than would be gained from an intercooler, not to mention the lack of a free flowing area in the rear areas of the Fiero for an inter-cooler.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||EdsB52||07-18-2001||07:28 PM||||I would recomend dealing with these guys at West Coast Fiero. I'm 90% sure I'm going to do a 3.4 swap in my 87 GT and I'm going to have these guys do the starter holes and whatever else I need. Give 'em a call, they're lots of help. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||gabriel||07-19-2001||06:43 PM||||Greets:<P>  For West Coast Fiero:<P>  What Haltech unit are you using?  They get kinda pricey, don't they? The last one I used cost well over a $1,100, and was a nightmare to install/program correctly.  <BR>             -g||||reg||1
Z||000006||West Coast Fiero||07-20-2001||12:16 PM||||Haltech E6GM, $500 done deal, an engine swap with this unit couldnt get any easier than putting Legos together ||||reg||1
